# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The leader agent's Caddyfile (internal/edge.Assemble)
#
# Caddy runs inside the agent. Assemble starts from this file, replaces the
# admin line with the agent's unix admin socket and storage, inlines every
# caddy/l4/*.conf of the state root in the layer4 block and every
# caddy/sites/*.conf at the import below. Nothing is imported from disk at
# load time.
#
# TLS strategy: wildcard certificate via Cloudflare DNS-01 challenge.
# This lets us get a single cert for *.home.<domain> without exposing
# port 80/443 to the public internet — the DNS challenge is entirely
# out-of-band.
#
# Docs:
#   https://caddyserver.com/docs/caddyfile/options
#   https://github.com/caddy-dns/cloudflare
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
{
	# Global ACME settings
	email {$ACME_EMAIL}

	# Obtain & renew ALL certificates via Cloudflare DNS-01.
	# The `cloudflare` directive comes from the caddy-dns/cloudflare module
	# compiled into the homelab binary.
	acme_dns cloudflare {$CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN}

	# Optional: use Let's Encrypt staging while testing to avoid rate limits.
	# Comment out for production.
	# acme_ca https://acme-staging-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory

	# Replaced by the agent's unix admin socket when assembled.
	admin localhost:2019

	# No automatic http→https redirects. :80 is the Cloudflare Tunnel's
	# listener, and the redirect for a tailnet-only site would answer a
	# tunnel client with that private hostname. Tailnet clients use https://
	# directly; unmatched plain-HTTP hosts hit the catch-alls below.
	auto_https disable_redirects

	# Raw TCP/UDP listeners (caddy-l4): one file per service with a port
	# declared as <listen>:<port>, e.g. gitea's ssh on :22 → gitea:2222.
	# Rendered by `homelab enable` alongside caddy/sites; they listen on the
	# agent's tailnet node only.
	layer4 {
		import /homelab/caddy/l4/*.conf
	}
}

# ── Wildcard TLS snippet ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Declare the wildcard cert once as a named snippet. Every tailnet site block
# (*.{$HOME_SUBDOMAIN}.{$DOMAIN}) imports it. Cloudflare sites are plain HTTP:
# TLS is terminated at the Cloudflare edge.
(wildcard_tls) {
	tls {
		dns cloudflare {$CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN}
	}
}

# ── Service sites ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One file per service, caddy/sites/<name>.conf, holding the site blocks of
# every layer it is enabled on (tailnet, Cloudflare). Rendered by
# `homelab enable|disable|reload <name>` from the service's exposure.yaml.
import /homelab/caddy/sites/*.conf

# ── Catch-alls for the plain-HTTP listeners ──────────────────────────────────
# cloudflared reaches Caddy on :80. A Host that matches no site there is
# closed rather than answered: without these, Caddy replies with an empty
# 200, and on :80 redirects private hostnames to https, which tells a tunnel
# client the names of tailnet-only services. Specific sites above win.
# :8081 is the onion listener a later Tor layer will use.
http://:80 {
	abort
}

http://:8081 {
	abort
}
